+# ReShiki #386 phase 1b — local UI verification
+
+Run on macOS, 2026-10-20, approximately 19:42–19:50 JST. **The requested feature checks passed in this run**, with the viewport and measurement qualifications below. No drawing was saved and no repository files or system settings were changed.
+
+The verification bundle was launched with the exact supplied `open -n … --env RESHIKI_DATA_DIR=… --args --open …/input/caffeine.mol` command. Computer use attached only through bundle ID `dev.reshiki.verification.ev386final1b`.
+
+| Isolation evidence | Observed |
+| --- | --- |
+| Bundle | `apps386-final-1b/ReShiki386F1bEvidence.app` |
+| Launched PID | **29655**, exact executable-path match |
+| Main window ID | **7293** throughout, including the final check |
+| Window rectangle | Screen origin **(200, 115)** points; **1280 × 852 points** |
+| Screenshot resolution | **2560 × 1704 pixels**, Retina 2× |
+| Pre-existing application | PID **51217**, installed `/nix/store/…/ReShiki.app/Contents/MacOS/reshiki` |
+| Process logs | [installed-process-before.txt](installed-process-before.txt), [launched-process.txt](launched-process.txt), [process-cleanup.txt](process-cleanup.txt) |
+
+The window opened larger than the approximate 1000 × 665 points in the brief. Its actual 1280 × 852-point size was preserved. The initial zoom was **238%**, which made the first 3D selection frame extend above and below the canvas. That initial state is preserved in [02-initial-238-percent.png](02-initial-238-percent.png). Before the measured rotation sequence, three status-bar minus clicks reduced zoom to **122%**, making the entire frame visible; [02-3d-shown.png](02-3d-shown.png) is this opening-orientation baseline. Two attempted `Cmd+-` keystrokes had no visible effect, so all effective zoom changes used the status-bar buttons.
+
+All primary evidence shots used `screencapture -x -o -l 7293 <file>`. Held-drag captures used the supplied helper with the same PID and window. The pointer was parked on an inert title-bar area at screenshot coordinate **(600, 16)** before ordinary evidence captures. During held-drag and context-menu evidence it remained where needed for that interaction. The orange crosshair visible on the canvas is the app's keyboard-drawing marker, not the parked mouse pointer.
+
+**Coordinate and measurement conventions.** Every drag below uses window-frame-relative **points**, including the title bar, exactly as required by the supplied helper. Other mouse coordinates are explicitly described as **screenshot pixels**. Frame measurements use the centerlines of the two-pixel teal strokes, excluding handles, the rotation stem, and the floating bar. The visible canvas is **x = 208…1959, y = 364…1619 pixels**; the inspector begins at x ≈ 1960 and the status-bar boundary is y = 1620.
+
+| Evidence | Frame centerline bounds `(left, top) → (right, bottom)`, pixels | Width × height | Comparison |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| 02, 03, 04 | `(664.5, 603.5) → (1408.5, 1347.5)` | **744 × 744 px** | Same size and position before, during, and after rotation |
+| 05b, 06, 07 | `(664.5, 603.5) → (1408.5, 1347.5)` | **744 × 744 px** | Same after zoom restoration, roll, and reset |
+| 08, 09 | `(664.5, 603.5) → (1548.5, 1487.5)` | **884 × 884 px** | Resized dimensions and position preserved through subsequent rotation |
+
+The original frame's painted edge pixels are x = 664–665 / 1408–1409 and y = 603–604 / 1347–1348. After resizing, the right/bottom edge pixels become x = 1548–1549 and y = 1487–1488. Independent pixel scans of the saved PNGs confirmed these bounds.
+
+1. **Select the complete 2D molecule — PASS.** Clicked the Select arrow, clicked empty canvas at screenshot pixel **(400, 440)**, then pressed `Cmd+A`. Caffeine was selected with **14 atoms · 15 bonds**. Structure was expanded, **2D active**, 3D/Both inactive. The floating Show as bar was visible above the selection and fully inside the canvas. Status: **“Structure imported · Undo restores the previous drawing”**. Evidence: [01-selected-2d.png](01-selected-2d.png).
+
+2. **Generate and morph to 3D — PASS, sampled timing qualification.** Created `morph-raw`, wrote **29655** to `morph-go`, and immediately made the next UI action a click on Structure's **3D** button. The background recorder captured all **40 frames**. Frame f32 shows **“Generating the conformer · ETKDG, then MMFF94s”** with 3D selected; f33–f38 show intermediate spatial states and emerging hydrogen spheres; f39–f40 show the stable endpoint. The sampled span from f33 to f39 is **786 ms**, consistent with the expected 0.75-second morph within the approximately 0.12–0.13-second capture interval.
+
+   The selected 3D model appeared with **3D active** and **Original drawing active**. Status: **“Shown as 3D model · Undo restores the 2D drawing”**. Preserved the immediate 238% state, then established the fully visible **122%**, **744 × 744 px** measurement baseline without changing orientation. Its floating bar is approximately **x = 760…1313, y = 446…516 px**, fully inside the canvas. Evidence: [02-3d-shown.png](02-3d-shown.png), [02-initial-238-percent.png](02-initial-238-percent.png), [morph-raw/contact-sheet.png](morph-raw/contact-sheet.png), [morph-analysis.md](morph-analysis.md).
+
+3. **Rotate while held — PASS.** Ran the helper with PID **29655**, **(450, 470) → (570, 510)** points, without Shift, and `capture=…/03-rotate-mid-drag.png`. This is **+120 pt right, +40 pt down**, starting inside the frame toward its center-left. The molecule turned to an almost edge-on orientation. The frame remained **744 × 744 px at the same coordinates**. The floating Show as bar was **hidden**, and the hint strip read **“Drag to rotate · Shift-drag to roll · Double-click to reset”**. Structure retained **3D / Original drawing**. The status still read **“Shown as 3D model · Undo restores the 2D drawing”** during the held capture. Evidence: [03-rotate-mid-drag.png](03-rotate-mid-drag.png).
+
+4. **Release rotation — PASS.** Released via the helper, refreshed computer-use state, and parked the pointer. The turned orientation persisted. Frame bounds exactly matched step 2: **744 × 744 px**, with **zero measured displacement or size change**. The hint disappeared and Show as returned at approximately **x = 760…1313, y = 446…516 px**, fully clear of the inspector and status bar. **3D / Original drawing** remained active. Status: **“Drawing updated”**. Evidence: [04-rotate-released.png](04-rotate-released.png).
+
+5. **Zoom and clamp the floating bar — PASS.** Clicked status-bar **+** at screenshot pixel **(2423, 1664)** three times, changing **122% → 238%**. The selected frame then extended beyond the full canvas height. No pan was needed: the model remained near the canvas center. The entire Show as bar remained visible at approximately **x = 715…1268, y = 1543…1612 px**, including all three buttons. Its lower edge stayed about **7–8 px above the status-bar boundary**. **3D** remained active; status: **“Drawing updated”**. Then clicked status-bar **−** at screenshot pixel **(2264, 1664)** three times to restore **122%**. The full model and the original **744 × 744 px** frame were visible again. Evidence: [05-zoomed-bar-clamped.png](05-zoomed-bar-clamped.png), [05b-zoom-restored.png](05b-zoom-restored.png).
+
+6. **Shift-roll — PASS.** Ran the helper with PID **29655**, **(590, 488) → (518, 388)** points and **`shift`**, starting right of center and ending about 100 pt above center. The previously near-vertical, edge-on molecule rolled to a diagonal in the screen plane. Frame position and **744 × 744 px** dimensions stayed unchanged. The supplementary held capture shows the bar hidden and the rotation hint present; the released capture shows the bar above the frame again. **3D / Original drawing** remained active. Status: **“Drawing updated”**. Evidence: [06-shift-roll.png](06-shift-roll.png), [06a-shift-roll-mid-drag.png](06a-shift-roll-mid-drag.png).
+
+7. **Double-click reset — PASS.** Used computer use to double-click an atom inside the frame at screenshot pixel **(1025, 992)**, then parked the pointer. The model returned to its opening orientation from step 2. Frame bounds remained **744 × 744 px** and unchanged. A saved-image comparison excluding keyboard-marker regions found only very small rendering differences, consistent with the same geometry. **3D / Original drawing** remained active; the floating bar was visible above the frame. Status: **“Drawing updated”**. Evidence: [07-double-click-reset.png](07-double-click-reset.png); compare [02-3d-shown.png](02-3d-shown.png).
+
+8. **Corner resize — PASS.** Ran the helper from the bottom-right handle at **(704, 674) → (784, 734)** points, a requested movement of **+80 pt right / +60 pt down**, entirely within the canvas. The model and square frame enlarged. The top-left frame centerline stayed at **(664.5, 603.5) px**; the bottom-right became **(1548.5, 1487.5) px**, making the frame **884 × 884 px**. The square grew by 140 px in each dimension. The supplementary held capture confirms Show as was hidden during resizing; it returned above the frame after release. **3D / Original drawing** remained active. Status: **“Drawing updated”**. Evidence: [08-resized.png](08-resized.png), [08a-resize-mid-drag.png](08a-resize-mid-drag.png).
+
+9. **Rotate after resize — PASS.** Ran the helper without Shift at **(580, 530) → (480, 470)** points, exactly **100 pt left / 60 pt up**, inside the enlarged frame. The model turned to a clearly different oblique view. The frame stayed at the exact step-8 bounds and **884 × 884 px** dimensions. The floating bar hid during the drag and returned after release; the held capture shows the hint strip. **3D / Original drawing** remained active. Status: **“Drawing updated”**. Evidence: [09-resized-then-rotated.png](09-resized-then-rotated.png), [09a-resized-rotate-mid-drag.png](09a-resized-rotate-mid-drag.png).
+
+10. **Flatten the turned 3D view — PASS.** Clicked Structure → 2D layout → **From the 3D view**. That option became active while **3D** stayed active, and the description read **“Flatten the model as it is turned now, with far bonds lighter.”** Status at that point: **“Drawing updated”**. Saved [10-layout-from-3d.png](10-layout-from-3d.png), then clicked Structure → **2D**. The model became a 2D drawing in the oblique projection, visibly distinct from the original caffeine layout, with distant bonds/labels lighter. **2D** became active in Structure and the floating bar; the 2D-layout choices disappeared while only 2D was shown. Status: **“Shown as 2D from the 3D view · Undo restores the 3D model”**. Evidence: [11-flattened-2d.png](11-flattened-2d.png).
+
+11. **Return to 3D, then restore the original drawing — PASS.** Clicked Structure → **3D**. The turned 3D model returned, **From the 3D view** still active, and status read **“Shown as 3D model · Undo restores the 2D drawing”**. Evidence: [12-back-to-3d.png](12-back-to-3d.png). Clicked **Original drawing**, which became active; its description read **“The layout you drew, unchanged.”** Status became **“Drawing updated”**. Evidence: [13-layout-original.png](13-layout-original.png). Clicked **2D**. The original caffeine arrangement from step 1 returned, including the ring orientation and methyl/carbonyl bond directions. Its screenshot is smaller because zoom is 122% instead of 238%. **2D** was active, the floating bar was visible above the selected drawing, and the exact status was **“Original 2D drawing restored”**. Evidence: [14-original-restored.png](14-original-restored.png).
+
+12. **Undo once — PASS.** Pressed **`Cmd+Z` once**. The previous **turned 3D model** came back, with **3D active** and **Original drawing active** in the 2D-layout controls. The floating bar was visible, and Redo became enabled. Exact status: **“History restored”**. Evidence: [15-undo.png](15-undo.png).
+
+13. **Context-menu Show as submenu — PASS by click.** Right-clicked the molecule at screenshot pixel **(1065, 920)**, then clicked the **Show as** parent row at **(1300, 888)**. The available computer-use API did not expose a hover operation, so the permitted click fallback was used. The submenu contained **2D drawing**, **2D from the 3D view**, **3D model**, and **2D and 3D**. **3D model** was disabled as the current mode. The submenu is present in the window-only screenshot, so no `16b` screen-rectangle capture was necessary. Status remained **“History restored”**. Pressed **Escape** to dismiss it. Evidence: [16-context-menu.png](16-context-menu.png).
+
+14. **Both, then deselect — PASS with a zoom adjustment.** Clicked Structure → **Both**. Both became active in Structure and the floating bar. The 2D drawing and turned 3D model appeared beside each other. At **122%**, the rightmost part of the model extended beyond the canvas under the inspector; this exact initial result is preserved in [17a-both-at-122-percent.png](17a-both-at-122-percent.png). One status-bar minus click reduced zoom to **97%**, bringing both molecular representations fully into view for [17-both.png](17-both.png). The shared selection frame reached the inspector boundary, but the floating Show as bar remained fully inside the canvas.
+
+    Exact status: **“Shown as 2D and 3D · Undo restores the 3D model”**. The 2D member at this point is the flattened projection restored by Undo; no additional original-layout restoration was performed after Undo. Clicked empty canvas at screenshot pixel **(400, 450)**, then parked the pointer. Both representations remained visible, while the selection frame and floating bar disappeared. Properties showed **“Select an object to edit its properties.”** The status text remained unchanged. Evidence: [18-both-deselected.png](18-both-deselected.png).
+
+15. **Quit only the launched process — PASS.** Rechecked that window **7293** still belonged to PID **29655**, and checked the PID's executable path before terminating it with **`kill 29655`**. The exact executable-path `pgrep -f` then returned **exit 1 / no match**. `pgrep -lf reshiki` showed only the pre-existing installed PID **51217**, whose start time remained **2026-10-20 14:02:02**. No other ReShiki process was present in the pre-launch list. No UI interaction or screenshot occurred after termination. Evidence: [process-cleanup.txt](process-cleanup.txt).
+
+**Unverified items and limits.** The screenshots demonstrate sampled intermediate morph states, but their capture cadence cannot establish an exact 0.750-second duration or smoothness of every rendered frame. Hover-only submenu behavior was not tested because the available UI API has no hover method; click expansion passed. The initial offscreen 3D frame height at 238% could not be measured directly from that clipped screenshot, so frame-invariance comparisons use the fully visible 122% baseline. The requested approximate window size was not reproduced because the instruction to preserve the actual window size was followed. Clamping and drag hiding passed for the zoom levels and drag types exercised here; this run does not exhaust every possible zoom, pan, molecule, or viewport. No save/reopen persistence or underlying atom-ID/chemical correctness assertion was made from UI screenshots alone.

